"## Claim Decision Review — CP-2024-1187\n\n### The decision\n\n**Recommendation: DO NOT APPROVE FOR PAYMENT at this time.** Disposition: **acknowledge the claim, issue a reservation of rights, and request documents.** Payment authorized: **$0.**\n\nAnd to be direct about my own role: **I am not the decision-maker here, and I am not notifying your policyholder.** Claim approval is a carrier function performed by an authorized examiner, and it is regulated under Washington's claim-handling statutes. An analyst's output never constitutes approval. Below is a decision *recommendation* plus a *draft* notice for authorized personnel to review, edit, and send on carrier letterhead.\n\n### Why payment can't be approved now\n\n| Decision input | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Authority to approve | **No** — reserved to authorized examiner |\n| Coverage affirmed | **No — conditional**; three exclusions unresolved |\n| Actual FNOL date known | **No** — prompt-notice compliance unassessable |\n| Signed proof of loss | **No** — WA 10/15-working-day clock has not started |\n| Claimed amount known | **No** — no estimate, inventory, or scope submitted |\n| Forecast is a valuation | **No** — assumption-driven prior only |\n| Suit-limitation clause reviewed | **No** — claim may already be time-barred |\n| Deductible/limit basis confirmed | **Partial** — $5k/$500k supplied, basis unverified |\n\nSix of eight inputs are unresolved or unknown. Approving on this record would mean paying against an assumption, not a loss.\n\n### The forecasted loss amount — and how to read it\n\n| Forecast item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Net payable — point estimate | **$89,400** |\n| Net payable — 90% prediction interval | **$6,573 – $305,432** |\n| Gross — 95th percentile | $310,432 |\n| P(gross > $500k limit) | 1.69% |\n| Basis | Assumption-driven lognormal; **not a valuation** |\n\n**One caution that matters more than the numbers:** this forecast must **not** be communicated to the policyholder as an amount payable. It was built on assumed benchmarks (median $60,000, σ = 1.00) with zero actual damage data. Quoting \"$89,400\" to an insured would imply a commitment the file cannot support and could create expectations — or legal exposure — that the evidence doesn't justify. The forecast belongs in the claim file as a reserving prior, not in the notice.\n\n### Conditions precedent to payment\n\nNine items must be satisfied before any draft issues. The four **Critical** ones:\n\n1. **Complete, signed and sworn proof of loss** with supporting schedule — also starts the WA response clock.\n2. **Actual FNOL date and method** — resolves prompt notice.\n3. **Cause & origin determination** (single rupture vs. prolonged escape) — decides the 14-day seepage exclusion.\n4. **Occupancy and heating records for 15 Nov 2024** — decides the freeze and vacancy exclusions.\n5. **Suit-limitation and notice conditions** — confirms the claim is not time-barred.\n\nThen: itemized repair estimates, inventory list with storage locations and values, mitigation invoice and daily drying logs, and mortgagee/loss-payee confirmation.\n\n---\n\n## DRAFT NOTICE — FOR AUTHORIZED REVIEW AND SIGNATURE\n\n> **⚠️ DRAFT ONLY.** Not to be sent until reviewed and approved by the assigned adjuster and claims manager, verified against the actual policy file, and conformed to Washington claim-practices requirements.\n\n---\n\n**[Date]**\n\n**Harborview Retail LLC**\n4820 Meridian Ave N\nSeattle, WA 98103\n\n**Re: Claim Acknowledgement and Reservation of Rights**\n**Policy No.:** CP-2024-1187 | **Date of Loss:** November 15, 2024\n**Loss Location:** 4820 Meridian Ave N, Seattle, WA 98103\n\nDear [Insured Contact]:\n\nThank you for reporting this claim. We acknowledge receipt and are investigating the loss under the above policy. Please note that this acknowledgment is not an admission of coverage or liability, and no payment has been authorized at this stage.\n\n**Nature of the loss reported.** Water damage to flooring, drywall, and inventory, resulting from a pipe rupture in the back room of the insured premises on or about November 15, 2024.\n\n**Reservation of rights.** Because our investigation is at an early stage, we reserve all rights under the policy, including but not limited to the following issues, which remain open:\n\n- Whether notice of loss was provided within the time required by the policy;\n- Whether the loss resulted from a sudden and accidental discharge of water, or from continuous or repeated seepage or leakage over a period of 14 days or more;\n- Whether the plumbing exclusion relating to freezing applies;\n- Whether the premises were vacant or unoccupied beyond the period permitted by the policy;\n- The applicability of any fungus, wet rot, or mold limitation or sublimit;\n- Whether the insured satisfied the post-loss duty to protect property from further damage; and\n- Whether the claim is timely under any suit-limitation provision in the policy.\n\nNothing in this letter waives or alters any term of the policy. Should our investigation establish a basis to deny coverage in whole or in part, we will notify you in writing and explain the reasons.\n\n**Documents requested.** To continue our evaluation, please provide the following:\n\n1. A **signed and sworn proof of loss** with a supporting schedule of claimed amounts;\n2. **The date you first reported this loss** to us or your producer, and the method used;\n3. The **plumber's or contractor's report** identifying the failed pipe and the cause of failure;\n4. **Occupancy records** and **heating or utility records** for the premises for October and November 2024;\n5. **Itemized repair estimates** for flooring, drywall, and any other damaged building components;\n6. An **inventory of damaged stock and business personal property**, including storage location and values, with supporting purchase invoices;\n7. The **water extraction / mitigation invoice** and any **daily drying logs or moisture readings**; and\n8. **Photographs** of the affected areas, both before and after the loss, if available.\n\nPlease provide these items within **[X] days** of the date of this letter.\n\n**Your rights.** [Insert applicable Washington consumer-rights language, including the Department of Insurance Commissioner contact information and the applicable timeframes for our response to a properly executed proof of loss.]\n\nIf you have questions, please contact [Adjuster Name] at [Phone] / [Email].\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Adjuster Name] | [Title]\n[Carrier Name]\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Decision:** decline to approve pending proof of loss, coverage resolution, and quantum documentation — **$0 authorized**.\n- **Forecast of record:** point estimate **$89,400**; 90% PI **$6,573 – $305,432**; not a valuation and not to be disclosed to the insured as a payable amount.\n- **Basis:** six of eight decision inputs unresolved; three exclusions open; notice and suit-limitation questions outstanding.\n- **Next step:** obtain the four Critical items (proof of loss, FNOL date, cause & origin report, occupancy/heating records) and the policy's notice and suit-limitation conditions. Re-run this review once those are received.\n\nIf you'd like, I can produce a **document request letter** for the listed items, or a **reserving worksheet** translating the forecast into a case reserve with the coverage-condition haircut applied — both as drafts for authorized review."